        "source": "pdf_layout",
        "field": "abstract",
        "raw_text": "In this work, we propose a simple framework of construct- ing efficient non-interactive zero-knowledge proof (NIZK) systems for all NP. Compared to the state-of-the-art construction by Groth, Ostrovsky, and Sahai (J. ACM, 2012), our resulting NIZK system reduces the proof size and proving and verification cost without any trade-off, i.e., neither increasing computation cost, CRS size nor resorting to stronger assump- tions. Furthermore, we extend our framework to construct a batch argument (BARG) system for allNP. Our construction remarkably improves the effi- ciency of BARG by Waters and Wu (Crypto 2022) without any trade-off.",
